From dece787dceff3c6472abd40df77cf46e8979f5d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [tier 1] hot-lend: more hot experts in the KV pool's free
 pages outside prefill

`KT_KV_HOT_LEND=1`: outside prefill the KV pool's free pages hold up to
`KT_KV_HOT_EXTRA` more experts a layer on the GPU on a shadow layer;
their routes go to the GPU and to the CPU at weight 0. The experts
leave whenever the pool needs the pages or a prefill starts.
`KT_KV_HOT_SPARE_FLOOR_MB` lets the slots also use idle driver memory
above the floor. Every rank holds the same slots (the CPU runs on rank
0 with its routing).

`KT_KV_HOT_DYNAMIC_SLOTS=1`: the slots follow what is routed. Route
counts every routed expert on the device; every 8 decode forwards,
outside the graph, each layer swaps held experts for better-scored ones
(decayed counts, half-life 256 forwards): out of the slot table at
once, copied in on a side stream from kt-kernel's zero-copy expert
arenas, into the table on the next round. Without it the slots hold the
placement's next-hottest experts, which a placement recorded on one kind
of text serves poorly for another (3-6% of the routes of code, JSON or
math for one recorded on Japanese prose).

Numerics: Not bit-identical: the lent experts run in the GPU MoE kernel
instead of kt-kernel, and which and how many are lent depends on the free
KV pages and the routing so far, so decode output depends on load and
history.

Prerequisites: `kv-vmm`, `prefill-lend`, `stream-prefill` (zero-copy, for
the dynamic slots), `kv-lend-plan`.

